hived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-04-23T16:37:29Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T14:31:23Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4, 4.4.1, 4.5 Dev 1 - 3\n\n### System information\n\nwin 10\n\n### Issue description\n\nUsing the AnimationPlayer with its Onion Skinning feature leads to weird behavior in combination with SpringBoneSimulators and a SpringBoneCollider.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cb70b08a-0873-43f3-b6a5-5d5021098da8\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Import an Armature with multiple attached bones\n2. import it to a scene\n3. add a SpringBoneSimulator Node to the Skeleton\n4. add a SpringBoneCollider Node to the Simulator\n5. Look at any animation in the player and activate OnionSkinning (skip to a frame with a bigger move to see a stronger effect)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[OnionskinningissueSpringBoneIssue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19872438/OnionskinningissueSpringBoneIssue.zip)\n\nThe 3D model is made by me. If anyone wants to use it, have fun","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105690/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105690/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinn